#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0504 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "PLAN-library-template-label-resolution R2-3 (owner 2026-10-04, follow the authority): CR504 covers every variable whose name ends in TM (the rule's own scope keeps its pre-plan 'but not DTM'), so this rule judges XSTM with its OWN fragment's phrase - label_template(\"LIBRARY\", stem=\"*TM\") is '{Time}' for it - although the longer *STM covers the name too and CDISC-AD0510 judges it as well. 'Start Moment' lacks 'Time' -> one violation, reported with the phrase this rule judged. XETM ends in ETM and its label carries 'Time'; XTM is the plain positive control. Under round 1 (longest-suffix governance) this rule did not judge XSTM."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#library variable-metadata ADLBC *TM name=*TM label="{Time}"
#library variable-metadata ADLBC *STM name=*STM label="{Start Time}"
#library variable-metadata ADLBC *ETM name=*ETM label="{End Time}"
#library variable-metadata ADLBC *DTM name=*DTM label="{Datetime}"
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt variable_name=XSTM variable_label="Start Moment" library_variable_label_template="{Time}"
dataset ADLBC class=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col XTM type=Char label="Analysis Time"
col XSTM type=Char label="Start Moment"
col XETM type=Char label="End Time"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALB | x | y | z
---
